1. Introduction to JavaScript
- JavaScript is a scripting language and part of programming languages.
- It is a high-level programming language.
- It is used to create interactive web pages by adding functionality to web pages.
- JavaScript is understood and executed by web browsers using JavaScript engines.
- JavaScript is a global language supported by all major browsers.
- JavaScript can be used on both the browser side and server side.
- It can work on both:
  - Frontend
  - Backend
Popular language: JavaScript is one of the most commonly used and popular programming languages today.

Frameworks and Libraries:
- Frontend: React.js, Angular.js, Next.js.
- Backend: Node.js, Express.js.

2. Why JavaScript?
JavaScript makes web pages interactive.

Without JavaScript:
- Web pages are static.
- They only display text and images.
- They do not respond when we click a button or type something.

With JavaScript:
- Dynamic features such as pop-ups, forms and animations.
- User interaction through clicks and scrolling.
- Works directly in the browser without needing extra software.
- JavaScript makes a website active instead of just looking like a book.

